course: dictionary
lesson: 15569
title: Susceptible: easily affected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Susceptible means easily affected, harmed or influenced by something. If you are susceptible to colds, you catch them quickly. «Babies are very susceptible to colds, so they need to be kept warm.» The sentence tells you babies get colds easily, and that is why they need extra warmth.
explain: You can also be susceptible to a way of being treated. «The crow was susceptible to flattery, so she believed every nice word the fox said.» Flattery means praise that is not really true. The crow was easily fooled by it, so susceptible means easily influenced.
explain: Susceptible is a formal word, so you will often see it with the word to after it: susceptible to something. Use the clue that follows «to». Susceptible to frost means easily harmed by frost. Susceptible to illness means likely to get ill.
fact: Susceptible means easily affected, harmed or influenced by something.
fact: Susceptible can also mean likely to catch an illness.
fact: Young children, old people and sick people are often more susceptible to illness.
fact: Some plants are susceptible to frost, so gardeners cover them on cold nights.
fact: In stories, a susceptible person is easily fooled or persuaded.
fact: «Highly susceptible» means very easily affected or influenced.
exercise: «Babies are very susceptible to colds.» What does susceptible mean here? | Able to sing very loudly | Fond of being outdoors | *Likely to catch a cold | Full of sunshine
exercise: «The crow was susceptible to flattery, so she believed every nice word the fox said.» What does susceptible mean? | Good at hiding | Easily bored | *Easily influenced or fooled | Able to fly very high
exercise: «Some plants are susceptible to frost, so Dad covers them at night.» Why does Dad cover the plants? | Because the plants are bored | To keep the sun away | *Because frost could easily harm them | To make the plants grow taller
test: «Old people are more susceptible to illness.» What does susceptible to illness mean? | Very rich | Never ill | Very good at games | *Likely to get ill
test: Which phrase is the best match for susceptible? | Fast asleep | In the garden | Very tall | *Easily affected or influenced
exam: «He is highly susceptible to praise, so every compliment makes him believe anything.» What does highly susceptible mean? | Always cold | *Very easily influenced | Not at all interested | Very quiet
